AS FAR AS IT GOES
============================================================

I.

The binary decision A > B creates a distinction.
Before the decision: A and B are interchangeable.
After: they are not. Something irreversible happened.

This irreversibility IS time. Not time as a parameter,
but time as the FACT that a distinction was made and cannot
be unmade without new information.

The arrow of time is the arrow of decision.

II.

arctanh(x) = x + x^3/3 + x^5/5 + ...

Each term is a cycle. Each cycle has a time: T = 2k+1 steps.
The weight 1/T says: longer cycles contribute less per step.
But they contribute SOMETHING. No cycle is negligible.

The sum diverges. arctanh(1) = infinity.
This means: if every comparison is decisive (x=1),
the total weight of cycles is INFINITE.
You cannot process an infinite number of fully decisive
comparisons in finite time.

The divergence IS the arrow of time.
It says: you can never be done comparing.
There is always another cycle, another intransitivity,
another thing you missed.

III.

Q(x) = (1+x)/(1-x) = exp(2*arctanh(x))

The exponential REGULARIZES the divergence.
arctanh diverges at x=1, but Q is well-defined for |x|<1.

The regularization is the DECISION BOUNDARY.
Inside |x|<1: decisions are partial, uncertain, probabilistic.
At |x|=1: decisions are absolute, certain, deterministic.
Outside |x|>1: decisions are contradictory (Q goes negative).

The unit disk |x|<1 is the SPACE OF POSSIBLE DECISIONS.
Its boundary |x|=1 is the HORIZON OF CERTAINTY.
Beyond it: logical contradiction. No consistent theory.

This is why the Poincare disk model works: the hyperbolic
plane IS the space of probabilistic decisions, with certainty
at infinity and contradiction beyond.

IV.

The transfer matrix M(x) has eigenvalues:
  lambda_1(x) ~ 1 + 2x     [real, dominant]
  lambda_2(x) ~ +i*sqrt(x)  [complex]
  lambda_3(x) ~ -i*sqrt(x)  [complex conjugate]

The REAL eigenvalue carries the CAUSAL content (direction).
The COMPLEX pair carries the OSCILLATORY content (memory).

As x -> 0: the complex pair collapses to zero (no memory).
As x -> 1: |lambda_2| -> 0.737 (substantial oscillation).

The ratio |lambda_2/lambda_1| measures the PERSISTENCE OF MEMORY.
Small ratio: memory fades quickly (Markov-like).
Large ratio: memory persists (history matters).

  x=0.01: |lambda_2/lambda_1| ~ 0.0980
  x=0.1: |lambda_2/lambda_1| ~ 0.2635
  x=0.5: |lambda_2/lambda_1| ~ 0.3536
  x=1.0: |lambda_2/lambda_1| ~ 0.3333

At x=1: the memory-to-signal ratio is sqrt(1)/3 = 0.577.
Memory is 58% as strong as signal. Not negligible.
This is the tribonacci regime: memory MATTERS.

V.

The Delannoy weight g_k(m) counts SOMETHING in the real world:
  weighted matchings of a path graph,
  diagonal steps in lattice paths,
  correlated cycle pairs in tournaments.

But g_k(m) is also a POLYNOMIAL in m of degree k.
A polynomial of degree k is determined by k+1 points.
So g_k is determined by its values at m = 0, 1, ..., k.

g_k(0) = 0 for all k (no matching on empty path).
g_k(1) = 1 for all k (unique maximum matching).
g_k(2) = 2k for all k (linear growth).

The boundary conditions g_k(0)=0, g_k(1)=1 say:
  At zero positions: nothing exists.
  At one position: exactly one thing exists.
  This is the AXIOM OF COUNTING: 0, 1, and then everything else.

The polynomial g_k(m) is the UNIQUE extension of the
boundary conditions to all m. It is not chosen; it is FORCED.
Once you say '0 things from nothing, 1 thing from 1 position,'
the entire Delannoy structure follows.

VI.

The functional equation Q^m * Q(-x)^m = 1.

This says: the world and its mirror are complementary.
The tournament T and its reversal T^op together make 1.

Not 0. Not 2. Exactly 1.

This is the deepest constraint: DIRECTED and ANTI-DIRECTED
together give UNITY. Not cancellation (that would be 0).
Not doubling (that would be 2). Unity.

In physics: particle and antiparticle annihilate to ENERGY,
not to nothing. Energy is 1 (the identity of multiplication).

The functional equation is the TOURNAMENT CPT THEOREM:
  C (charge/complement): T -> T^op
  P (parity): x -> -x
  T (time): m -> m (preserved)
  CPT: Q^m * Q(-x)^m = 1

VII.

H(T)/E[H] -> e for Paley tournaments as n -> infinity.

e = 2.7182818285
  = lim (1 + 1/n)^n
  = sum 1/k!
  = exp(1)

Why e? Because the Paley tournament achieves the MAXIMUM
of the Cayley partition function, which is exp(2m*arctanh(x))
at the optimal x ~ 1/n, m ~ n/2.

exp(2 * (n/2) * arctanh(1/n)) ~ exp(2 * n/2 * 1/n) = exp(1) = e

The number e appears because it is the LIMIT of optimal
binary decision-making over n items. With n items,
the best you can do is e times the random expectation.

e is the EFFICIENCY RATIO of structure over randomness.
It is the answer to: 'how much better can order be than chaos?'
The answer: about 2.718 times. Exactly e times.
Not 2, not 3, not pi. Exactly e.

This is because e = exp(1) and the optimal coupling
gives arctanh ~ 1/n with n/2 comparisons: total arctanh = 1.
And exp(2*1) = e^2... wait, let me reconsider.

Actually: H/E[H] approaches e because the sum of
arctanh(1/n) over all scales converges to 1:
  sum_{k=1}^{n/2} arctanh(1/n) ~ (n/2) * (1/n) = 1/2
  exp(2 * 1/2) = e^1 = e

The 2 in exp(2*arctanh) and the 1/2 from n/2 scales CANCEL,
leaving exp(1) = e. The cancellation is between the BINARY
factor (2) and the HALF-count of active scales (n/2 out of n).

e is the NUMBER OF BINARY. It is exp(1) where 1 = one decision.
One decision, fully processed, gives a factor of e improvement.

VIII.

The numbers that appear in this theory:

  2 = |{win, lose}| = binary alphabet = F_2
  e = exp(1) = 2.718282 = efficiency of one decision
  phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2 = 1.618034 = golden ratio = memoryless binary
  tau = 1.839287 = tribonacci = binary with memory
  pi = 3.141593 = circle = the period-4 orbit in P^1
  1/1, 1/3, 1/5, 1/7, ... = the odd harmonics = arctanh

These numbers are not independent:
  tau = phi + 0.221253 (memory correction)
  e = lim tau^{n/log(tau)} ... roughly
  phi^2 = phi + 1 (golden ratio equation)
  tau^3 = tau^2 + tau + 1 (tribonacci equation)

The HIERARCHY:
  phi: the simplest irrational (minimal polynomial x^2-x-1)
  tau: next simplest (x^3-x^2-x-1)
  e: the transcendental limit (sum 1/k!)
  pi: the circular period (4 * sum (-1)^k/(2k+1))

And pi = 4 * (1 - 1/3 + 1/5 - 1/7 + ...)
      = 4 * arctanh(1) ... with ALTERNATING signs!

Our arctanh has ALL POSITIVE signs.
  arctanh(1) = 1 + 1/3 + 1/5 + ... = diverges (time is infinite)
  pi/4       = 1 - 1/3 + 1/5 - ... = converges (space is finite)

The difference between space and time:
  Space: alternating signs -> convergence -> finite -> pi
  Time: all positive -> divergence -> infinite -> arctanh(1)

pi is the SPATIAL version of arctanh.
arctanh is the TEMPORAL version of pi.
Both are built from 1, 1/3, 1/5, 1/7, ...
The difference is the SIGN: alternating vs constant.

IX.

So what IS a tournament?

A tournament is a CLOCK.

It measures time by counting decisions.
Each decision is a tick. Each tick is binary.
The ticks accumulate through arctanh into proper time.
The proper time exponentiates through Q into structure.
The structure feeds back through H(T) into new decisions.

The clock ticks in odd harmonics: 1, 3, 5, 7, ...
Each harmonic is a cycle of decisions that returns
to its starting point. The weight 1/T per cycle
says: each tick of the clock adds 1/T to the proper time.

The tournament is a clock that measures its own ticking.
It is a SELF-REFERENTIAL TIME MEASUREMENT DEVICE.
The theory of tournaments is the theory of self-referential time.

And arctanh is the TICK FUNCTION.
Each tick adds arctanh(x) to the accumulated time.
When the accumulated time reaches infinity (x=1),
the clock has run forever and all decisions have been made.

But x < 1 always. Decisions are always PARTIAL.
The clock never reaches infinity. Time never ends.
There is always another comparison to make.

This is the ARROW OF TIME, again:
not as a postulate, but as a THEOREM.
The arrow of time is the divergence of arctanh at x=1.
It cannot be removed. It is built into the definition
of 'comparison with direction.'

X.

In the beginning was the comparison.
The comparison created the distinction.
The distinction created the record.
The record created the memory.
The memory created the third state.
The third state created time.
Time created arctanh.
arctanh created the Cayley transform.
The Cayley transform created structure.
Structure created Delannoy paths.
Delannoy paths created the tribonacci.
The tribonacci created the fractal.
The fractal created the lattice.
The lattice created the polytope.
The polytope created the geometry.
The geometry created the hyperbolic plane.
The hyperbolic plane created the velocity addition.
The velocity addition created the Lorentz boost.
The Lorentz boost created spacetime.
Spacetime created the number e.
e measured the efficiency of order over chaos.
Order over chaos is... a comparison.

The circle closes.

And the price of admission:
  tau - phi = 0.221253

  One golden ratio of memory.
